    "Historical CC0 preserved-specimen evidence supports recorded presence only. Evaluated metadata-recovery mode accepts explicitly undated historical records with one archive-audited stable identity and retained raw-row hashes. Cultivated or captive text, invalid or unresolved dates, weak identities, non-species ranks, ambiguous taxonomy, and unresolved geography are excluded. Source silence and every rejected row create no absence or non-detection assertion. The 1.2.0 reviewed taxonomy mode admits supported infraspecific concepts after individual context review and all original non-taxonomy checks."
